  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 岩\ntitle: rock; boulder\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 山\nradicalNumber: 46\nonyomi: [ガン]\nkunyomi: [いわ]\ndistractors: [山, 各, 含]\n---\n\n# 岩 — rock; boulder\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 山 (no. 46) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n岩 いわ is a rock or boulder. 岩塩 がんえん is rock salt or halite, using the on reading ガン. The complete compound names a mineral substance, not an instruction to pronounce standalone 岩 がん.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See [山](山.md), mountain, above [石](石.md), stone, and imagine a large exposed rock. This is a modern-shape mnemonic rather than a claim that every rock belongs to a mountain.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ガン | on | 岩塩 がんえん - rock salt; halite |\n| いわ | kun | [岩](../words/岩.md) いわ - rock; boulder |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [岩](../words/岩.md) いわ - rock; boulder\n- 岩塩 がんえん - rock salt; halite\n- [溶岩](../words/溶岩.md) ようがん - lava, including solidified lava\n\n## Notes\n\n- Compare [石](石.md), stone. English rock and stone glosses overlap, so do not infer a strict size boundary from the mnemonic.\n- 岩塩 uses ガン + エン. The えん belongs to [塩](塩.md) here, not to 岩.\n- Keep the upper 山 when distinguishing the full character from 石 alone.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1217270, 1217280, 1546120.\n",
